line":27},{"title":"Playing haptics","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/playing-haptics","line":27},{"title":"A screenshot of the Measure app on iPhone showing a bunch of carrots. A line segment extends from one end of a carrot to the other end. The measurement is four and a half inches.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/8a3faa907452d5fdb2771a64ffdcdb62/augmented-reality-measure-carrots%402x.png","line":35,"embedded":true},{"title":"Providing coaching","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Providing-coaching","line":45},{"title":"Handling interruptions","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Handling-interruptions","line":47},{"title":"`ARCoachingOverlayView`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ARKit/ARCoachingOverlayView","line":47},{"title":"An illustration of an iPhone screen showing the corner of a room viewed through the camera. On the screen is a translucent overlay containing the surface-detection indicator. The indicator is a white square with rounded corners projected into the 3D space. A small iPhone is shown scanning back and forth along the base of the square. A circle of dots trailing the iPhone emphasizes the movement.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/a8f541f789d28879cd0d2c9862cbdcba/augmented-reality-coaching-overlay%402x.png","line":49,"embedded":true},{"title":"Helping people place objects","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Helping-people-place-objects","line":55},{"title":"An illustration of a complex visual placement indicator consisting of a circular shape with markers indicating a center and diameter, inside right-angle shapes framing a square. The indicator is shown in 3D perspective with the longest edge on the bottom.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/b5533e905940a2c62239bc80b16dbc46/augmented-reality-app-specific-indicator%402x.png","line":59,"embedded":true},{"title":"`ARTrackedRaycast`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ARKit/ARTrackedRaycast","line":61},{"title":"Designing object interactions","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Designing-object-interactions","line":69},{"title":"An illustration showing a cube and a hand with the index finger touching the cube. There's a curved line intersecting the finger and cube to indicate the movement of the finger to the right as it directly manipulates the object.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/e68ef4f9413642524873ee66cd4bba4e/augmented-reality-user-interaction-direct%402x.png","line":73,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration showing a cube. Below the cube are two buttons, each with a circular arrow pointing in the opposite direction, offering indirect ways to rotate the cube.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/dcd7ceea5314b22c0bb24dfe45008651/augmented-reality-user-interaction-indirect%402x.png","line":75,"embedded":true},{"title":"Gestures","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/gestures","line":77},{"title":"An illustration showing a sphere. The base of the sphere is on a grid. Two lines that are parallel to the grid and perpendicular to each other pass through the center of the sphere. There's an arrow at the tip of each line, indicating movement direction across the two-dimensional surface of the grid.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/d0ac02ed21a0af9534631b63c824b9d7/augmented-reality-plane-movement%402x.png","line":81,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration showing a sphere. A dotted line runs vertically through the center of the sphere. An arrow wraps around the outside of the sphere and the vertical line, from left to right, indicating the ability to rotate the sphere around the line.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/0c40f98719aee4f83f34e9255fac4f29/augmented-reality-axis-rotation%402x.png","line":83,"embedded":true},{"title":"Offering a multiuser experience","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Offering-a-multiuser-experience","line":99},{"title":"`isCollaborationEnabled`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ARKit/ARWorldTrackingConfiguration/isCollaborationEnabled","line":101},{"title":"Occluding virtual content with people","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ARKit/occluding-virtual-content-with-people","line":103},{"title":"`isCollaborationEnabled`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ARKit/ARWorldTrackingConfiguration/isCollaborationEnabled","line":105},{"title":"Reacting to real-world objects","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Reacting-to-real-world-objects","line":107},{"title":"Detecting Images in an AR Experience","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ARKit/detecting-images-in-an-ar-experience","line":109},{"title":"Communicating with people","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Communicating-with-people","line":117},{"title":"An illustration of a cube. The base of the cube is indicated with a grid, and the active side of the cube is outlined in blue. Arrows follow a continuous circle around the cube to the right, hinting that the cube can be rotated within the 3D context.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/43871ef4bb55592e7474b1905da12f98/augmented-reality-3d-hint%402x.png","line":130,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration of a cube. The base of the cube is indicated with a grid, and underneath the cube is the word Rotate, hinting that the cube can be rotated within the 3D space.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/d60c7354a3ed6528ea35765cd86a970c/augmented-reality-2d-hint%402x.png","line":132,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration of an iPhone screen in landscape orientation showing the corner of a room viewed through the camera. In the room are two AR objects: a desk and a chair. Each object has a label attached to the object by a vertical line. The label in each object ends with a greater-than sign to indicate the label can be tapped for more information.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/341d2c982c2042c369769344be588e6f/augmented-reality-labels%402x.png","line":138,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration of an iPhone screen in landscape orientation showing a full-screen view with the detailed information for a chair. On the left side of the screen is an image of the chair, in the middle is a vertical separator line, and on the right is the model number, price, and size of the chair.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/3dcd4c7352111a30f5fab8370b060836/augmented-reality-popover%402x.png","line":142,"embedded":true},{"title":"Handling interruptions","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Handling-interruptions","line":146},{"title":"Managing Session Life Cycle and Tracking Quality","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ARKit/managing-session-life-cycle-and-tracking-quality","line":148},{"title":"An illustration of an iPhone screen showing the corner of a room viewed through the camera. On the screen is a translucent overlay containing the surface-detection indicator. The indicator is a white square with rounded corners projected into the 3D space. A small iPhone is shown scanning back and forth along the base of the square. A circle of dots trailing the iPhone emphasizes the movement.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/f39344a998cd544223592f8b13c118fb/augmented-reality-vertical-orientation%402x.png","line":152,"embedded":true},{"title":"Suggesting problem resolutions","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Suggesting-problem-resolutions","line":162},{"title":"An illustration showing a corner of a brightly lit office that contains a desk and chair.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/13887c5129d1c8add4ff07c5b0ba86e5/augmented-reality-sufficient-lighting%402x.png","line":166,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration showing a corner of a dark office that contains a desk and chair.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/346b5de0b7f08b0a510192cae8189cab/augmented-reality-insufficient-lighting%402x.png","line":168,"embedded":true},{"title":"Icons and badges","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Icons-and-badges","line":178},{"title":"Resources","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/resources/#ios-apps","line":180},{"title":"The AR glyph.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/05428c411e6c937857838da1fa944416/augmented-reality-glyph%402x.png","line":182,"embedded":true},{"title":"A button containing the AR glyph and the text View in AR.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/5df46e31e22d0b25d2ad1a5e6342eb1d/augmented-reality-glyph-button%402x.png","line":184,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration that shows the AR glyph centered within a frame that represents the minimum clear space to leave around the glyph.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/4a22c5126bd05f8291ab3637b01c89b9/augmented-reality-glyph-minimum-clear-space%402x.png","line":190,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration of a partial iPhone screen. On the screen is an app with four gray squares in a grid layout, each containing a picture of a vintage toy: one robot, and three rocket ships. In the upper left corner of each square is the AR badge with the glyph and the text AR.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/ebffaa99bc0113cb9c94f8cf5da94ace/augmented-reality-badging%402x.png","line":194,"embedded":true},{"title":"Resources","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/resources/#ios-apps","line":196},{"title":"The AR badge with both the glyph and the text AR.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/65ae0b4baf76d633cb247880b2c4f338/augmented-reality-badge-iconandtext%402x.png","line":198,"embedded":true},{"title":"The glyph-only AR badge.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/807119fbf8f1c62a35dddde3fdc0a026/augmented-reality-badge-icon%402x.png","line":200,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration of the AR badge with the AR glyph and text AR. A frame surrounds the badge to indicate leaving clear space around the badge.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/ac95fbcb89cd066b471e15c74e0475b4/augmented-reality-badge-iconandtext-clear%402x.png","line":210,"embedded":true},{"title":"An illustration of the glyph-only AR badge. A frame surrounds the badge to indicate leaving clear space around the badge.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/6b63f2ad4df182c7be792b90e56abec7/augmented-reality-badge-icon-clear%402x.png","line":212,"embedded":true},{"title":"Platform considerations","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#Platform-considerations","line":214},{"title":"visionOS","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/augmented-reality#visionOS","line":218},{"title":"custom gestures","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/gestures#Designing-custom-gestures-in-visionOS","line":220},{"title":"immersive experience","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/immersive-experiences","line":220},{"title":"permission","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#visionOS","line":220},{"title":"ARK